A Galactic Union Year, or GUY, is a standard unit of time measurement in the [[Galactic Union]], and in ''[[Final Frontier]]'' as a whole. It is equivalent to about 3.945 or <math>\frac{288}{73}</math> [[Earth]] years. The GUY is used by most spacefaring species as a convenient method of communicating time, as time is usually divided into unique units depending on the planet. Each GUY is divided into 32 semesters with 45 equinoxes each. In total, 1 GUY is equal to 1440 equinoxes.

The calendar system begins at 1-1, 0 GUY, which is when the Galactic Union was founded. Dates before the GU’s inception are marked with a negative (-) GUY value; e.g. -142 GUY would be 142 GUYs before the GU's inception.

