===Notable conversions===
Aside from the standard GU system, individual planets and factions might have their own local systems based on solar or lunar revolution.

1 GUY is equivalent to:

*3.945 or <math>\frac{288}{73}</math> [[Earth]] years
*1.365 or <math>\frac{789}{578}</math> [[Lama'entria]] years
*4.069 or <math>590\over145</math>Ottori years

==Calendar==
[[File:Calendar blue.png|thumb|The GUY calendar, with 5 rows and 9 columns.|alt=|400x400px]]
The GUY standard calendar is formatted with 5 rows and 9 columns. Each group of 9 equinoxes is 1 week, and there are exactly 5 weeks per semester. Weeks are not official GU time units but are often used by the common people for convenience. Unlike the Earthen calendar, there are no leap days or leap years; every subdivision is static and does not change. This is necessary to keep the calendar system simple and consistent throughout the large expanse of the Galactic Union, and the Milky Way as a whole.

Each week consists of 9 equinoxes: Turkal, Rezet, Ever, Rimbo, Overt, Elena, Mono, Eflo, and Rinns. The names of the days of the week are arbitrary, and are abbreviated in the calendar with the letters T-R-E-I-O-L-M-F-N. Officially, the 32 semesters do not have names, and are usually referred to by number; for example, the twelfth semester in a GUY might be written "S12" or "Sem12".
